// #2913: the BARE `iter_length` predates the qualified iteration protocol --
// `xs |> iter_length` inside a `[C: Iterator[T]]` combinator used to compile to
// a bare call that had to exist in the merged program. The checker still
// admitted the spelling while nothing lowered it, so it ICE'd in codegen.
fn main() -> Unit allows Stdout {
  println(Int::to_string(iter_length([1, 2, 3])))
}
